INTERPRETATION
Every negative individual slice occurs at K=3, where the exact Pell
calculation and terminal reflection argument prove cumulative
nonnegativity for all prefixes.  For K>=4, every audited individual
slice is nonnegative and every endpoint-ratio minor points in the
descent direction of Target 5A8H28R8.  The 100-by-100 run is bounded
evidence for that ratio target, not its proof.  All 29,596 incidence
identities hold.  The fully looped Turan minors and the even-time
incidence sandwiches have no negative value, as required by Target
5A8H28R9.  Lemma 5A8H28AF now proves the fully looped Turan
inequality unboundedly.  All 14,453 normalized Turan-reserve steps are
nonnegative; this is bounded evidence for Target 5A8H28R11, not its
proof.  All 571,924 parity-compatible Schur branch steps are
nonnegative; this is bounded evidence for Target 5A8H28R12, not its
proof.  The 99 off-parity failures, beginning with value -1 at
(K,d,j)=(4,1,1), certify that the parity restriction is genuine.  The
negative mirror pair is an exact obstruction to proving the terminal
prefix by independent symmetric slice pairs, and the degree-seven
incidence value 4 disproves the stronger alternating sandwich.

